      "line": 332,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "When were hydrothermal vents discovered?",
          "1977, Galapagos Rift, DSV Alvin"
        ],
        [
          "What energy source do vent bacteria use?",
          "H₂S oxidation (thioautotrophy)"
        ],
        [
          "How does *Riftia* carry H₂S without dying?",
          "Special hemoglobin with separate H₂S-binding site; no competition with O₂"
        ],
        [
          "What do ANME archaea do?",
          "Anaerobically oxidize methane using sulfate — prevent seafloor CH₄ from reaching atmosphere"
        ],
        [
          "What are cold seeps?",
          "Continental margin sites where methane + sulfide-rich fluids seep through sediment"
        ],
        [
          "Why does this matter for astrobiology?",
          "Enceladus and Europa plumes suggest similar chemistry — life without sunlight is plausible"
        ],
        [
          "What is the Lost City?",
          "Mid-Atlantic alkaline hydrothermal field driven by serpentinization, not volcanism"
        ],
        [
          "What is the growth rate of *Riftia pachyptila*?",
          "Up to 85 cm/year — fastest of any marine invertebrate"
        ]
      ]
    }
